{
  "_doc": [
    "The vocabulary the generator names the description's records, enums and fields with (src/Zabbix.Generator/ZabbixNames.cs).",
    "A field whose C# name is the mechanical capitalisation of its wire name (sortorder -> Sortorder) is named by its words instead",
    "(SortOrder); a record or enum name's capitalised parts are named the same way (ActionOperationOpgroupRequest ->",
    "ActionOperationGroupRequest, ValuemapMappingType -> ValueMapMappingType, DsvcStatus -> DiscoveredServiceStatus), a word the",
    "part before it already ends in said once (Operation + OperationGroup is OperationGroup, Map + MapElement is MapElement).",
    "An enum member is named the same way (ITEM_TYPE_HTTPAGENT: Httpagent -> HttpAgent, ZBX_PREPROC_LTRIM: Ltrim -> LeftTrim).",
    "Applied once, when the description is read (ApiDescription.Read): the records, the clients, the cmdlet parameters, the views",
    "and the type converters all see the same name; the old name is not kept as a cmdlet parameter alias. A name the overlay",
    "(schema/overlay.json) chose is made of known words and stays as it is. Each part is split into the fewest known words (a",
    "whole word wins over its pieces: timeline stays Timeline); a part that does not split keeps the old capitalisation, and",
    "ZabbixNamesTests lists every such part, so a new compound fails the build until this file learns its words.",
    "words: known words, rendered capitalised. expansions: abbreviations and Zabbix shorthands, rendered as written (op is an",
    "action operation, hk housekeeping, selement a map element, usrgrp a user group, passwd a password, dsvc a discovered",
    "service, the Zabbix documentation's terms); where the overlay already spells a word (EvalType, AuthType, CalcFunction,",
    "EscalationPeriod, Unique, ZIndex) the rendering follows it. names: whole wire parts named outright (opdata is a trigger's",
    "operational data, not an operation's; bool2dec is a preprocessing step's BooleanToDecimal)."
  ],
